.TH DUPLICACY-FUSE 1 "November 2026" "duplicacy-fuse" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
duplicacy-fuse \- browse Duplicacy snapshot revisions through a read-only FUSE mount
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B duplicacy-fuse
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.P
.B duplicacy-fuse mount
.BR --repo " " DIR
.BR --revision " " NUMBER
.RI [ --revision " " NUMBER ... ]
.BR --mountpoint " " DIR
.RI [ options ]
.P
.B duplicacy-fuse history
.BR --repo " " DIR
.BR --path " " PATH
.RI [ options ]
.P
.B duplicacy-fuse revisions
.BR --repo " " DIR
.RI [ options ]
.P
.B duplicacy-fuse clear-cache
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B duplicacy-fuse
mounts selected Duplicacy snapshot revisions as a read-only filesystem and
provides commands for listing snapshot revisions and file or directory history.
Mounting reads snapshots through the embedded Duplicacy Go library. History and
revision commands use the external Duplicacy command-line client.
.P
Run a command with
.B --help
to print its available flags. Flags use the Go command-line parser syntax; a
flag value may be supplied after the flag or after an equals sign.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B mount
Mount one snapshot revision or compare multiple revisions. The mount runs in the foreground by default.
.TP
.B history
List the revisions containing a file, or use
.B --directory
to check the history of an exact directory path.
.TP
.B revisions
List the available revisions for the selected snapshot.
.TP
.B clear-cache
Remove the Duplicacy FUSE chunk cache.
.TP
.B gui-storages, gui-snapshots, gui-revisions, gui-browse
Private JSON and IPC helpers for the companion desktop application. These
interfaces are not intended for direct interactive use.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
The following options are available for
.BR mount ,
.BR history ,
and
.BR revisions .
.TP
.BI --repo " DIR"
Repository directory. Required.
.TP
.BI --storage " NAME"
Configured storage name. If exactly one storage is configured, it is selected
automatically; otherwise this option is required.
.TP
.BI --snapshot " ID"
Snapshot ID to select. Defaults to the snapshot ID configured for the selected
storage.
.TP
.BI --password " PASSWORD"
Storage-encryption password. Prefer Duplicacy's password environment variable
instead of putting a password in process arguments. This is not the SMB login
password.
.SH MOUNT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --path " PATH"
Repository-relative file or directory to expose at the mount root. If omitted,
the repository root is exposed. Repeat this option to select multiple paths;
it is repeatable for comparison mounts.
.TP
.B --compare
Force the revision-folder comparison layout, including when only one revision
and one path are selected. This is used by comparison profiles in the GNOME
companion; ordinary one-revision mounts retain their existing layout.
.TP
.BI --revision " NUMBER"
Positive snapshot revision to mount. Required and repeatable. When multiple
revisions or paths are supplied, each revision with at least one matching path
is exposed beneath a top-level folder named with its revision and UTC timestamp.
Selected paths retain their repository-relative hierarchy; selected directories
include their subtrees. Paths are matched exactly without rename inference.
Missing selected paths are omitted, and setup fails if no selected path exists
in any requested revision. Metadata for each requested revision is loaded during
setup, so startup time and metadata memory use grow with the number and size of
selected revisions.
.TP
.BI --mountpoint " DIR"
FUSE mountpoint directory. Required.
.TP
.BI --cache-dir " DIR"
Persistent chunk cache directory. Defaults to
.IR ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/duplicacy-fuse/chunks .
Choose a location outside both the repository and backup storage.
.TP
.BI --cache-size " SIZE"
Maximum persistent chunk cache payload size. Defaults to
.BR 10GiB .
Accepts a non-negative byte count with an optional
.BR B ,
.BR KB ,
.BR MB ,
.BR GB ,
.BR KiB ,
.BR MiB ,
or
.B GiB
suffix. Decimal suffixes use powers of 1000 and binary suffixes use powers of
1024. A value of zero disables persistent chunk-payload caching.
.TP
.B --debug
Log mount timings, directory scans, chunk reads, and cache activity. Debug
output can include repository paths and directory names.
.TP
.B --background
On Linux, start a detached mount and return once FUSE initialization completes.
The mount process writes its log to a mode-0600 file under the system temporary
directory.
.TP
.BI --gui-control-fd " FD"
Private socket descriptor used by the companion desktop application. Do not
invoke this option manually.
.SH HISTORY OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --path " PATH"
Repository-relative file or directory whose history is requested. Required.
Absolute paths and paths escaping the repository are rejected.
.TP
.B --directory
Report the revisions where the exact directory exists. Without this option,
history is for a file and the repository root cannot be selected.
.TP
.B --json
Write machine-readable JSON instead of the default tabular or Duplicacy output.
.TP
.BI --duplicacy-bin " PATH"
External Duplicacy CLI executable. Defaults to
.BR duplicacy .
.SH REVISIONS OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Write machine-readable JSON instead of tab-separated revision and timestamp
lines.
.TP
.BI --duplicacy-bin " PATH"
External Duplicacy CLI executable. Defaults to
.BR duplicacy .
.SH CLEAR-CACHE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --cache-dir " DIR"
Chunk cache directory to clear. Defaults to the standard user cache directory.
Only directories marked as a
.B duplicacy-fuse
cache are cleared.
.SH DESKTOP HELPER OPTIONS
The
.B gui-storages
helper accepts
.BR --repo .
The
.B gui-snapshots
helper accepts
.B --repo
and
.BR --storage .
It accepts but ignores
.BR --snapshot ,
and rejects
.BR --password .
The
.B gui-revisions
helper accepts the repository selection options documented above, except that
it rejects
.BR --password .
.P
The
.B gui-browse
helper accepts the repository selection options, a positive
.BR --revision ,
and an optional repository-relative
.BR --path .
It returns immediate directory entries as JSON over the private helper socket
and rejects
.BR --password .
All helpers requiring storage access use the private
.BI --gui-control-fd " FD"
socket descriptor supplied by the desktop application. Do not invoke this
option manually.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DUPLICACY_PASSWORD
Storage-encryption password for the default Duplicacy storage. For a named
storage, Duplicacy uses
.B DUPLICACY_<STORAGE_NAME>_PASSWORD
with the storage name uppercased and non-alphanumeric characters replaced by
underscores. Duplicacy's own configuration and password behavior apply to
external CLI commands.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory used for the default chunk cache when set.
.SH NOTES
All mounts are read-only. The mount process requires access to
.B /dev/fuse
and the FUSE2
.B fusermount
helper. The CLI-backed commands require a Duplicacy CLI on
.BR PATH ,
or its path can be supplied with
.BR --duplicacy-bin .
.P
The cache stores downloaded chunk payloads as plaintext. Protect custom cache
locations accordingly. File history, revision listing, and directory-history
revision discovery run the external Duplicacy CLI with the selected repository
as its working directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Mount revision 42 at a local mountpoint:
.P
.RS
.nf
duplicacy-fuse mount --repo /backup/repo --revision 42 \\
  --mountpoint /mnt/duplicacy-history
.fi
.RE
.P
Show JSON history for a file:
.P
.RS
.nf
duplicacy-fuse history --repo /backup/repo --path src/main.go --json
.fi
.RE
.P
List revisions for a named storage:
.P
.RS
.nf
duplicacy-fuse revisions --repo /backup/repo --storage nas
.fi
.RE
.P
Compare files and a directory across two revisions:
.P
.RS
.nf
duplicacy-fuse mount --repo /backup/repo --storage nas \
  --revision 41 --revision 42 --path src/main.go --path docs \
  --mountpoint /mnt/duplicacy-comparison
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fusermount (1),
.BR duplicacy (1)
